// Lucius Orbius, quartermaster of the depot at Noviodunum. Cut Brigodunon's
// tally five years ago. Decent inside the machine. Three of the ways out go
// through him: his mercy, his price, or Dannotalos's claim.
=== start
[flag orbius_met] -> again
~ set orbius_met
A long room full of boxes, every one with a number painted on it. A brazier, a table, two stools, a bald man with ink on the side of his hand, coughing into a cloth. He folds the cloth and puts it away before he looks up.

[flag nov_interpreter] "Ah. The interpreter. The sentry sent a boy running; I'm told you read Gallic." His Latin is soft and quick. "Sit down, sit down. I have four hundred names in this depot and I can spell eleven of them."
[flag letter_shown] "Dannotalos's man." His Latin is soft and quick, his Gallic slow and bad. "Dagolitos sent word. I wondered when one of you would come to look at the merchandise."
[flag nov_visitor] "A visitor." His Gallic is slow and bad, and he knows it. "Family. We get some. Not many." He looks at you a moment. "Not many."
[flag depot_sneaked] He looks at your legs, mud to the knee, and then at your face. "You didn't come through my gate," he says in bad Gallic. "No. Well. You're here now. Sit, before the watch sees you standing about."
[!flag nov_interpreter, !flag letter_shown, !flag nov_visitor, !flag depot_sneaked] "Yes?" His Gallic is slow and bad, and he knows it.
-> hub

=== again
[flag orbius_done] -> after
He coughs, folds the cloth, looks up. "Yes?"
-> hub

=== after
[flag orbius_mercy] "Go away," he says, not unkindly. "You were never here. Three children died of fever. I have it in writing."
[!flag orbius_mercy] "Our business is done." He doesn't look up.
* "Goodbye." -> END

